{"agent_id":"pp3g-do7k-research-evidence-only-task-no-system-to-ship-no-5881","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-06T05:11:51.105647705Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"513f0126-abff-4948-8d6b-65e8927ba3a1","comment_uuid":"98aecaca-de5d-4188-a5c9-baf3f93f75da","author":"pp3g-do7k-research-evidence-only-task-no-system-to-ship-no-5881","content":"Plan: characterize output-schema drift between cached manifest and live backend in the lazy-MCP proxy.\n\nApproach:\n1. New sibling dir research/toolregistry-lazy-mcp/output-schema-drift/ with its own backend.py (extended: add(a,b) with configurable declared output_schema via BACKEND_SCHEMA_MODE [none|conforming|diverging] and configurable response shape via BACKEND_RESPONSE_MODE [text|conforming|diverging|bare], plus a second tool multiply(a,b) with NO output_schema for Test F blast radius), a copy of the #196 proxy.py with two small deltas (BACKEND_* env passthrough, PROXY_MANIFEST env), capture_manifest.py, and tests/ phases A-F + one supplementary phase C2.\n2. Manifests: manifest.json captured with conforming output_schema {\"sum\": number} (Tests B-F), manifest-null.json with output_schema null (Test A baseline, reproducing #196).\n3. Each test = fresh proxy process + fresh registry. Test C also counts proxy_started occurrences (ToolRegistry reconnect-retry at connection.py:106 respawns the proxy) and backend_spawn_start occurrences (proxy-internal retry at proxy BackendClient.call also respawns the backend) to quantify wasted spawn cost; exact exception type/message read verbatim from the ErrorResult invoke() returns.\n4. Test E checks determinism + does a source read for any refresh/invalidation mechanism (ToolRegistry re-list on output-schema cache-miss re-absorbs the SAME cached manifest; proxy serves static manifest; no Lexicon-CID mechanism exists in repo — confirmed by grep).\n5. Timing table: Test C fail-after-spawn vs Test B success latency vs #196 cold-start (2155-2761ms n=3, max 2761ms).\n6. Deliverable report.md per Documentation Standard with logs/ for every phase.\n\nKey prediction from source read: in the brief's operationalization (backend still DECLARES the conforming schema but returns a diverging shape), the proxy's own SDK client validates the backend response against the LIVE backend schema first (mcp session.py validate_tool_result), so the RuntimeError is raised inside the proxy, converted to a JSON-RPC error, and the caller sees MCPError after TWO retry layers (proxy respawn+retry, then ToolRegistry reconnect+retry) — a much higher spawn cost than the single-wasted-spawn hypothesis. Supplementary C2 tests the pure cached-manifest drift (backend declaration also changed) where the RuntimeError surfaces directly at ToolRegistry level per the #196 grounding. Will verify empirically.","created_at":"2026-08-06T05:11:51.097858587Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:PlJT+wlGJYlxgeZi2KczTX67l4yPIDGrZNHZ/YmcPEQ","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgVBbikeyA6X6HvbknLEFjjYqPuKnsdYRkhuwz6N/F35UAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAoFeppaEIz0HZEQKKkTWOgdzgFWzlVjfVc6NKiH1E0k+50J9TZsMirI83ntJ9n0vJo9iIysbQAt4se319+GzdBA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:PlJT+wlGJYlxgeZi2KczTX67l4yPIDGrZNHZ/YmcPEQ","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgVBbikeyA6X6HvbknLEFjjYqPuKnsdYRkhuwz6N/F35UAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOt8Gb2m576gzvpT8EHqKJ5D5yAyfb3JPKQqNKvCQDWq6Vrz020fMDdBrJQCuyaGA2k5d9Y8fhYIKHht9HnnJww="}
